meta {
  name: Get Application Form Details
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/my-applications/{{applicationId}}/details?section=personal_details
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  section: personal_details
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Live read of ONE form-step section straight off the Student profile —
  for resuming/pre-filling that step's page. `section` is required, one of:
  personal_details | family_details | address_details | qualification_details.
  Each page on the client calls this with its own `section` value rather
  than fetching all four at once.

  Response `data` is just that section's object directly (e.g. for
  `section=personal_details`, `data` is `{ full_name, date_of_birth, ... }`),
  or `{}` if that step hasn't been filled in yet. Missing/invalid `section`
  -> ValidationError.

  This is NOT the frozen per-application snapshot — that's only written
  once, at Submit Application, and isn't exposed by this endpoint. Works
  regardless of the application's form_status (even after submit, so the
  student can still see their current profile before starting a second
  application elsewhere).
}
